    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d26">

                <pb facs="0278" n="20" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg20"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1599</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-17T17:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 17, 1915, 5 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 7 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>216. British Ambassador not apprehensive Austria and Italy will come to terms.
                    This also my opinion. Things seem smoothing down. Italy prepared, tested new
                    siege guns yesterday, but many think no hostile move will occur before end
                    April. Personally I think likely if she moves it will be without much
                    warning.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
